{"id":11899,"date":"2025-02-18T18:51:44","date_gmt":"2025-02-18T18:51:44","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=11899"},"modified":"2025-08-20T15:10:18","modified_gmt":"2025-08-20T15:10:18","slug":"portlands-guide-to-remodel-historical-home","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/portlands-guide-to-remodel-historical-home\/","title":{"rendered":"Portland&#8217;s Guide on How To Remodel a Historical Home"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;<strong>How to Plan for a Historical Home Remodel in Oregon and What Are Your Options<\/strong>&#8220;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Oregon&#8217;s historical homes are treasures that tell the city\u2019s story. From the iconic Craftsman bungalows of Irvington to the Victorian beauties of Ladd\u2019s Addition, these homes embody timeless charm. Yet, planning a remodel for a historical property requires careful consideration of preservation rules, compliance with <strong>Oregon permits<\/strong> and <strong>Oregon code<\/strong>, and thoughtful design to maintain the home\u2019s character.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In this guide, we\u2019ll explore how to plan for a historical remodel in Oregon, your options for upgrades and restorations, and how the <strong>Oregon pre-construction process<\/strong> simplifies the journey.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/AD_4nXchVQFxhhf6rxQIvu9YhDmHiSD_HeUN8uz5tOi8XqEWGkIQjNuMAxAyJHqUmQSFqk3YPIDEuCizU1JhYX56zB9bD4Lx_7yyB8MVqeo5ttMv32egpaIDu4YJQXG8dkFARsn7mwIeHw.png\" alt=\"historical home\" class=\"wp-image-11903\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Understanding Your Historical Home and it&#8217;s Status<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before diving into a remodel, it\u2019s important to understand your home\u2019s historical status. Some homes are in designated historic districts or conservation zones, which require adherence to specific guidelines.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Historical Designations in <strong>Oregon <\/strong><\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Local Historic Districts<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Homes in neighborhoods like Irvington or Ladd\u2019s Addition must meet city preservation standards for exterior changes.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>National Register of Historic Places<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Homes listed on the National Register may be eligible for preservation grants but come with stricter guidelines.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Conservation Zones<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Properties in conservation zones have less restrictive rules but still require compliance for visible changes.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How to Determine Your Home\u2019s Status<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check your property\u2019s designation through the Oregon Bureau of Development Services or consult with the Oregon Historic Landmarks Commission.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Assess Your Historical Home\u2019s Needs and Goals<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Historical homes often require a balance between preservation and modernization. Start by identifying the most pressing updates alongside your desired upgrades.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Common Needs in Historical Homes<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>System Upgrades<br><\/strong>Replace outdated plumbing, electrical wiring, and HVAC systems to meet modern safety standards and <strong>Oregon code<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Structural Repairs<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Address foundation issues, sagging floors, or roof repairs to ensure long-term stability.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Hazard Mitigation<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Safely remove lead paint or asbestos commonly found in older homes.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Goals for a Historical Remodel<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Maintain original features like crown molding, built-ins, or stained-glass windows.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Modernize kitchens and bathrooms while keeping them in harmony with the home\u2019s character.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add energy-efficient upgrades without disrupting the aesthetic.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Explore Your Options for a Historical Home Remodel<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A historical remodel can range from small restorations to significant renovations. Here are the options available to Oregon homeowners:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Preservation<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Focus on restoring original features to their former glory without significant alterations.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Examples<\/strong>: Refinish original hardwood floors, repair vintage windows, or restore decorative plasterwork.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Renovation<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Update outdated systems and interiors while maintaining the home\u2019s historical charm.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Examples<\/strong>: Add a modern kitchen with period-appropriate cabinetry or update a bathroom with vintage-inspired fixtures.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Expansion or Addition<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add square footage while ensuring the new space complements the original architecture.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Examples<\/strong>: A second-story addition with matching materials or a rear extension that blends seamlessly with the existing structure.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com\/docsz\/AD_4nXczASlsUB5ARIhzaWqcNpK7KNZ856iuNxWBE560WJoXaVYhWT2fLt8-PxsJ77xCiJr5RFhwC8uBB8tO3eM4v8Wwe-vsdod3_ZGQ1j6ZkRb8_4uUxRDaZuccxld9TIaQ3qvh0FUwzA?key=gfqit43RTcpDqG6SOdS1go-6\" style=\"\" alt=\"planning and budgeting\"><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Plan Your Budget and Timeline<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Historical remodels often require a higher budget and longer timeline than standard projects due to the complexities involved.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Budget Considerations<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Plan for 10\u201320% more than your estimated costs to account for unexpected challenges like structural repairs or material sourcing.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Research grant programs or tax incentives for historical preservation. The<a href=\"https:\/\/restoreoregon.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> Restore Oregon<\/a> organization offers resources for homeowners.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Timeline Considerations<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The permitting and approval process can add months to your timeline.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sourcing historically accurate materials may involve longer lead times.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Navigate the Oregon Permits Process<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The permitting process for historical homes involves more steps than standard remodels to ensure compliance with preservation rules and <strong>Oregon code<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Steps for Obtaining Permits<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Historical Review<br><\/strong>Submit plans to the Oregon Historic Landmarks Commission for approval.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Building Permits<br><\/strong>Apply for permits through the Oregon Bureau of Development Services.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Inspections<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Schedule inspections during and after construction to ensure compliance.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How the Oregon Preconstruction Process Helps<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">During preconstruction, contractors handle permit applications, coordinate with preservation boards, and ensure all plans meet local regulations, saving you time and stress.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Work with the Right Professionals<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Hiring professionals experienced in historical remodels is critical to ensuring your project is successful.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What to Look for in a Contractor<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Proven experience with historical remodels in Oregon.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Knowledge of preservation guidelines, <strong>Oregon permits<\/strong>, and <strong>Oregon code<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong relationships with suppliers for sourcing period-appropriate materials.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Verified Quote<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u201cHistorical remodels are about more than construction\u2014they\u2019re about storytelling. Choose a contractor who understands the history of your home and can honor it during the remodel.\u201d \u2014 <em>Oregon Historic Landmarks Commission Representative<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Execute Your Historical Home Remodel with the Pre-construction Process<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <strong>Oregon pre-construction process<\/strong> is an essential step for planning and executing a successful historical remodel. This phase ensures all details are addressed before construction begins.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Steps in the Pre-construction Process<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Initial Consultation<\/strong>: Collaborate on goals, budget, and scope.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Site Evaluation<\/strong>: Identify potential challenges like outdated wiring or structural issues.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Design Development<\/strong>: Create detailed plans that balance preservation with modernization.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Permit Preparation<\/strong>: Navigate the permit process to ensure compliance.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Budget Planning<\/strong>: Develop a realistic budget, including contingencies for unexpected challenges.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Case Studies<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Case Study 1: Modernizing a Craftsman in Irvington<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A family updated their Craftsman home with modern plumbing, a redesigned kitchen, and restored wood detailing. Using the preconstruction process, their contractor navigated the permitting process and sourced custom cabinetry that matched the original 1920s style.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Case Study 2: Expanding a Victorian in Ladd\u2019s Addition<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Homeowners added a rear extension to their Victorian home, creating a modern open-concept kitchen and dining area. The new addition used reclaimed wood and period-appropriate finishes to blend seamlessly with the original structure.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Resources for Historical Remodels<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Oregon Historic Landmarks Commission<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/restoreoregon.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Restore Oregon<\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Oregon Bureau of Development Services<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/savingplaces.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">National Trust for Historic Preservation<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Conclusion: Respect History, Build Your Future<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Planning a historical remodel in Oregon requires patience, expertise, and a deep appreciation for the past. By understanding your options and leveraging the <strong>Oregon pre-construction process<\/strong>, you can preserve your home\u2019s character while creating a space that meets your modern needs. <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\">Contact us today<\/a><\/strong> to learn how we can guide you through every step of your historical remodel, from planning and permits to construction and completion. Let\u2019s bring your vision to life while honoring Oregon&#8217;s rich architectural heritage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>&#8220;How to Plan for a Historical Home Remodel in Oregon and What Are Your Options&#8220; Oregon&#8217;s historical homes are treasures that tell the city\u2019s story. From the iconic Craftsman bungalows of Irvington to the Victorian beauties of Ladd\u2019s Addition, these homes embody timeless charm. Yet, planning a remodel for a historical property requires careful consideration [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":11902,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[36,38,33,39],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-11899","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-general","category-remodel","category-remodeling-tips","category-resources"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/11899","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=11899"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/11899\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13072,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/11899\/revisions\/13072"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=11899"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=11899"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=11899"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}